        <definition>static&lt; T &gt; Lazy&lt; Optional&lt; T &gt; &gt; org.xvm.util.Lazy&lt; T &gt;.ofNullable</definition>
        <argsstring>(Supplier&lt; T &gt; supplier)</argsstring>
        <name>ofNullable</name>
        <qualifiedname>org.xvm.util.Lazy.ofNullable</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>Supplier&lt; T &gt;</type>
          <declname>supplier</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Creates a thread-safe lazy Optional that wraps nullable supplier results. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Use this instead of sentinel values (like 0L or -1) to represent &quot;no value&quot;.</para>
<para>The supplier may return null, which will be wrapped as <javadoccode>Optional.empty()</javadoccode>. Non-null values are wrapped as <javadoccode>Optional.of(value)</javadoccode>.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Example - replacing sentinel value patterns:</heading>
</para>
<para><preformatted><javadoccode>
// Before (using 0L as sentinel - bad because 0L could be valid):
private long timestamp;
public long getTimestamp() {
    if (timestamp == 0L) {
        File f = getFile();
        if (f != null &amp;&amp; f.exists()) {
            timestamp = f.lastModified();
        }
    }
    return timestamp;
}

// After (proper separation of &quot;not computed&quot; vs &quot;no value&quot;):
private final Lazy&lt;Optional&lt;Long&gt;&gt; timestamp = Lazy.ofNullable(() -&gt; {
    File f = getFile();
    return f != null &amp;&amp; f.exists() ? f.lastModified() : null;
});

public Optional&lt;Long&gt; getTimestamp() {
    return timestamp.get();
}
</javadoccode></preformatted></para>
