        <briefdescription>
<para>Creates a supplier that caches the result for a specified duration. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>After the duration expires, the next call will recompute the value.</para>
<para>This is useful for values that should be refreshed periodically, such as configuration or external resource state.</para>
<para>Note: This returns a <javadoccode>Supplier&lt;T&gt;</javadoccode> rather than <javadoccode>Lazy&lt;T&gt;</javadoccode> because the value can be recomputed multiple times.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>supplier</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the supplier whose result should be cached </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>duration</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the length of time to cache </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>unit</parametername>
